BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Parallax View (1974)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261112T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261112T210500
DTSTAMP:20261113T030000Z
UID:the-parallax-view-2026-11-12-19:00:00-08:00
DESCRIPTION:After a presidential candidate is assassinated\, political rep
 orter Joe Frady begins to suspect that the mysterious Parallax Corporation
  may be involved. As he investigates\, others who share his suspicions sta
 rt turning up dead\, including his editor\, Bill Rintels. Eventually\, Fra
 dy uncovers a conspiracy bigger than anyone expected and must race to prev
 ent the corporation’s next big hit as this political thriller plays out 
 in an explosive game of cat and mouse.\n\nAlan J. Pakula\, United States\,
  1974\, 102 min\, in English\n\nhttps://nwfilmforum.org/films/the-parallax
 -view/\n\nEstimated start: 19:20
LOCATION:Northwest Film Forum\, 1515 12th Ave\, Seattle\, WA 98122
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tokyo Story (1953)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261128T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261128T181000
DTSTAMP:20261128T233000Z
UID:tokyo-story-2026-11-28-15:30:00-08:00
DESCRIPTION:A profoundly stirring evocation of elemental humanity and univ
 ersal heartbreak\, Tokyo Story is the crowning achievement of the unparall
 eled Yasujiro Ozu. The film\, which follows an aging couple’s journey to
  visit their grown children in bustling postwar Tokyo\, surveys the rich a
 nd complex world of family life with the director’s customary delicacy a
 nd incisive perspective on social mores. Featuring lovely performances fro
 m Ozu regulars Chishu Ryu and Setsuko Hara\, Tokyo Story plumbs and deepen
 s the director’s recurring theme of generational conflict\, creating wha
 t is without question one of cinema’s mightiest masterpieces.\n\nYasujir
 ō Ozu\, Japan\, 1953\, 137 min\, in Japanese with English subtitles\n\nht
 tps://nwfilmforum.org/films/tokyo-story/\n\nEstimated start: 15:50
LOCATION:Northwest Film Forum\, 1515 12th Ave\, Seattle\, WA 98122
END:VEVENT
